Workstream ID: focus-playlist-link
Title: Add an optional thumbnail link to the supplied focus playlist
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Let users choose external study music without disturbing focus work
Dependencies: focus-room
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/29
Purpose: Add the user-supplied thumbnail and YouTube playlist to the compact
  focus-session card and full focus room. Clicking opens the playlist in a
  new tab. Do not embed a player, start audio, upload data or change sessions.
  Keep the feature local for review; do not publish source or the image.

Tasks:
  [x] Read compact/full focus controls and current runtime/privacy boundaries.
  [x] Derive a lightweight local thumbnail from the supplied image.
  [x] Reuse one external-link component on both focus surfaces.
  [x] Qualify thumbnail loading, safe new-tab navigation and network isolation.
  [x] Verify timer/state/report preservation and compact/full responsive access.
  [x] Update focused documentation, original tracking and owned continuity.
  [x] Prepare the preserved current-source preview for local review.

Acceptance criteria:
  Both focus surfaces show a real local thumbnail linked to the supplied
    playlist ID PLYw_q6Wu9DTU; no invented or substituted media destination.
  The whole card is mouse/touch/keyboard usable, names YouTube and the new tab,
    and uses noopener/noreferrer. Sharing-only URL tracking is not required.
  No YouTube iframe, API, thumbnail fetch, preconnect or autoplay is added.
    CareerOS makes no external media request before the user chooses the link.
  Existing timer controls and material errors remain before optional music.
    Short/narrow focus rooms keep core timer/report/close controls reachable.
  Opening the link does not reset/pause/complete a timer or write progress,
    reports or preferences. The provider controls playback after navigation.
  The app keeps its original tab; native fullscreen remains browser-controlled.
  The local supplied-image derivative has reserved dimensions and no retained
    source metadata. No third-party artwork or audio is generated or fetched.
  Existing schemas, focus controller, safeguards and prior local work remain.
  No owner profile, new image inspection, source commit/push/deployment.
  Technical verification remains separate from human review and media rights.

Completion evidence:
  Shared FocusPlaylist is a plain anchor with a locally bundled image.
  Supplied PNG1672x941/2023761bytes becomes WebP720x405/61336bytes locally.
  Public URL fetch returned the title DeepWorkCrossing; this is not listening,
    exhaustive playlist validation or a guarantee of provider availability.
  Strict build and17native cases/17attempts/one worker/no retries pass on
    unchanged348inputs08df6e8bdb35dc402508fe8e67a31b21007840cd94234adf2eebc9d137863251.
  Five playlist cases cover both themes/four viewports, local image/network
    isolation, keyboard/image clicks, safe new tabs and running/tutorial data.
    Twelve existing focus safeguards/layout/fullscreen cases also pass.
  Two earlier15/2diagnostics are retained: real0.75px nearest-scroll clipping
    fixed with scroll clearance; retained short-room scrolling fixed by
    resetting only the center panel on opening. Strict assertions are unchanged.
  Proof: docs/tracking/2026-11-27-focus-playlist-local-review.json.
  Human review and supplied-image publication rights remain unverified.

Completion log:
  2026-11-27 - Optional compact/full playlist is technically qualified locally.
